id: ops-restart-prepare
title: Restart daily prepare when main advances before request
description: A queued daily release loses its day when main advances during prepare or before request. Restart fresh preparation at the current main head without retargeting verified artifacts.
type: Issue
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[2]: "area:release","gh:unbraind/pm-ops#286"
created_at: "2026-11-16T19:47:45.672Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-17T02:00:11.347Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: "Advanced main restarts full build, verification, changelog and candidate preparation without caller changes; at most two bot workflow_dispatch runs per caller on main per release calendar day; owner dispatches ignored; publishedToday blocks restart; history/read/pagination errors fail closed with an explicit workflow error; dispatch sends only ref main and never retirement inputs; configuration digest unchanged; reconcile-only, retirement and recovery remain unchanged; unit and workflow contracts cover history, default retirement and permissions."
comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-16T19:49:29.476Z",codex-sol,"Root cause: prepare requires its refreshed main to equal the original trigger SHA, and request separately rejects a changed prepared base after runner queueing. Both correctly reject stale artifacts but lose the daily opportunity. Choose bounded caller workflow_dispatch (maximum two restarts), because a prepare-only loop cannot cover the separate request queue. Existing callers grant actions: write. A dedicated restart job retains read-only prepare and uses trusted workflow tools; redispatch preserves original dispatch inputs and increments prepare-restart-count. Each new run performs complete preparation at its new trigger SHA. Live GitHub publication dates block restarts after publishedToday. Scheduling counter is excluded from the durable configuration digest. Evidence: GitHub documents workflow_dispatch as a GITHUB_TOKEN recursion exception and Actions write as the dispatch endpoint permission. PR #291 is open; this work starts from main c29fe88 and is independent of its pending npm version logic."
  "2026-11-16T19:54:08.505Z",codex-sol,"Implementation: both existing refusal guards emit the rejected base before failing. A separate restart_prepare job runs despite failed/skipped dependencies, reads live current main and complete paginated publication dates, then redispatches the caller on main with all original workflow_dispatch inputs and counter +1. Two restarts maximum; malformed or dropped counters fail closed. Existing prepare/read and request/write permissions and recovery code are preserved. The caller template, self-pilot and migration examples now declare and forward the counter; consumer adoption requires that small caller change as well as the released workflow pin. Rejected attempts stay failed with a restart summary. Initial focused run found three old contract assumptions (only string/boolean inputs and installation in all new jobs); adjusted contracts to include numeric inputs and prove restart_prepare performs no npm installation. Typecheck, test-source typecheck and lint passed; expanded targeted regressions and changelog verification are running."
  "2026-11-16T19:55:21.576Z",codex-sol,"Expanded targeted regressions passed: 99 tests, zero failures or skips. The unmodified changelog gate exposed a one-line existing date mismatch: v2026.11.15 was committed/tagged on 2026-11-16, while its rendered heading still said 2026-11-15. Regeneration changes only that heading to the actual tag-commit date; no release content or version changes. This small generated correction is included so the required changelog gate can pass. Added fail-closed validation of malformed publication-date responses before final linked gates."
  "2026-11-16T19:56:31.817Z",codex-sol,"Final linked gates: pm test ops-restart-prepare --run --progress passed all five commands: npm run typecheck; npm run build:test; npm run lint; node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/release-prepare-restart.test.ts test/daily-release.test.ts test/daily-release-workflow.test.ts test/release-workflow.test.ts test/release-continuation.test.ts test/release-permissions-docs.test.ts (99 passed, zero failed/skipped); npm run changelog:check. npm run build regenerated committed text dist. Linked-test result persistence is disabled by existing tracker policy, so results are recorded in this comment. Full suite remains delegated to CI. Existing shared-runner hold is honored before push."
  "2026-11-16T19:57:06.004Z",codex-sol,"Implementation and linked evidence committed as 8cf3ea6 (fix: restart daily preparation when main advances). Additional npm run verify:release-changelog-date passed. All requested local gates passed, 99 targeted tests passed, and no release workflow was dispatched or rerun. Open limitations: consumer callers must adopt the numeric dispatch input/pass-through alongside the released workflow pin; rejected attempts remain failed while the dispatched attempt prepares afresh; full CI is pending. PR #291 remains independent. Releasing the claim for orchestrator review without closing the item."
  "2026-11-16T20:04:18.686Z",codex-sol,"Continuing PR #293 at 9ea21d7 after orchestrator review. Existing branch and remote agree; preserve the accepted immutable redispatch design and replace the caller counter with a fail-closed, timezone-aware daily bot-dispatch history bound. No caller changes or retirement inputs will be required. PR #291 remains open; pending-version planning remains independent."
  "2026-11-16T20:07:14.268Z",codex-sol,"Implemented input-free caller redispatch. The daily bound reads this caller workflow main-branch workflow_dispatch history since local midnight, counts triggering_actor.login with actor.login fallback only for github-actions[bot], and refuses after two bot runs. Pagination totals, duplicate identities, malformed evidence and read failures refuse with ::error::. Live publication cap remains before dispatch. Removed counter input, forwarding, documentation and digest exclusion. Fixtures cover history pages, owner actors, publication cap, DST and non-hour offsets; restart job retains contents read and actions write only."
  "2026-11-16T20:09:55.309Z",codex-sol,"Final source verification passed: npm run build; npm run typecheck; npm run build:test; npm run lint; node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/release-prepare-restart.test.ts test/daily-release.test.ts test/daily-release-workflow.test.ts test/release-workflow.test.ts test/release-continuation.test.ts test/release-permissions-docs.test.ts (104 passed, zero failed/skipped/canceled/TODO); npm run changelog:check; npm run verify:release-changelog-date. All six linked gates also passed via pm test ops-restart-prepare --run --progress. Tracker test-result recording is disabled, so this comment preserves the observed results. Caller workflows and digest calculation match the pre-counter base. Full-suite CI remains unverified; no workflow was dispatched or rerun."
  "2026-11-16T20:10:13.259Z",codex-sol,"Revision committed as 81a1876db4d7043e1a584ce459b002c88ca72851 on the existing PR #293 branch, on top of 9ea21d7 without rewriting history. All required targeted gates passed (104 tests, zero failed or skipped); PR body will describe history-based bounds and no caller migration. Releasing the claim for orchestrator verification; item remains in progress and must not be closed here. Remaining verification: remote CI and orchestrator review; no live restart was dispatched during development."
  "2026-11-17T01:46:21.440Z",codex-sol,"Review AB: verified original actor precedence is reversed and the executable CLI block lacks coverage. Will fix actor attribution and cover parsing, summary output, refusal exits, and file-level uncovered branches without changing thresholds."
  "2026-11-17T02:00:10.125Z",codex-sol,"Review AB verified and fixed PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64NWTK and PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64NWTd: original actor wins over rerun actor; owner-rerun regression refuses a third bot dispatch. CLI environment parsing, summary/stdout and failure exits now covered, including actual subprocess invocations. File-level focused report is 100/100/100/100; direct npm run coverage passes unchanged per-file 100 thresholds. Typecheck, build:test, lint, changelog:check and release regression tests pass. Linked touched tests pass 13/13. The initial linked coverage duplicate timed out at its snapshotted 120-second default; stored timeout corrected to 1200 seconds. Direct full coverage is the completion evidence. Pagination remains bounded by the stable 1000-record total, with a ten-page regression."
